594	/// What one bundled-encoder export costs (spec §11 CX-18): its resident peak, which the
595	/// Export Queue's limit books (`ExportEncoderLedger`), and its time, which the export
596	/// sheet's estimate reads. Two tables keyed alike, each figure carrying its source.
597	///
598	/// **Both are measured, never guessed, and both are a table edit to replace.** The figures
599	/// are `tools/proof/encoder_memory_measure.py`'s, recorded in `archive/codec-export.md`'s
600	/// "## C6a" and "## C6b" (`vp9_alpha_webm`'s first in "## C5"'s fix pass): one fresh Release
601	/// instance per key and size, the resident peak above the instance's own after a warming
602	/// frame, and the export's wall time. The TIME figures are C6b's: on an idle machine, the
603	/// GH5 4K clip on a 25 fps canvas, the median of three runs per key and size over 250 and
604	/// 50 frames, which separate the fixed start from the per-frame time. A MEMORY figure is the
605	/// larger of C6a's (C5's) single run and C6b's peaks, its source naming the run that won.
606	///
607	/// A figure is given at 1920 × 1080 and 3840 × 2160 and read at an export's pixels:
608	/// proportionally below 1080p, linearly through both points above it, extrapolated past 4K.
