808	/// Pass one of an export: read the composed mix and MEASURE it (`Loudness.swift`).
809	///
810	/// This is `Exporter`'s own "Measuring the mix" section, in a file of its own
811	/// because `Exporter.swift` went past app/CLAUDE.md's ~600-line cap when phase
812	/// 5 put a second pass in it. It is a MOVE and nothing else — the same methods,
813	/// the same order, the same bodies — so `Exporter.swift`'s five internal members
814	/// (`lock`, `measuring`, `scratchStorage`, `scratchCapacity`, and the
815	/// `isCancelled` / `setMeasureProgress` accessors over that lock) are internal
816	/// only to be reachable from here. Stored properties cannot live in an
817	/// extension, which is the whole reason the split is where it is.
818	///
819	/// **What it buys.** Every export that carries sound gets a measured
820	/// "Peak −1.0 dBTP · −14.0 LUFS" on its final line, and an export that asked to
821	/// be normalised gets the gain that lands it on its target. The pass is a
822	/// reader with no writer, no video output and no encoder — audio decode through
823	/// the plan's own mix, and nothing else — so it costs a few per cent of a movie
